        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-15T16:58:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "how about using the top of the 32 bit word as a counter of the used bits (as was done in Brian\u0027s Cl)?\n\nIn this case zero in that space would mean the original version with only two bits active.\n\nThe way it is suggested now we\u0027d need two bis for every new informational bit included in the word",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 259,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 259,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "f5ff45111b7ffdd64c57cb8a63355a61897ab872",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "381c9d02_cbd0b147",
        "filename": "include/ccd_config.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 259,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-15T19:37:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is only an 8-bit field, so we don\u0027t have room for a bit counter.\n\nWe could add another field, but then we have to bump the encoding version number, and ti50 would still need to support both encoding versions for a while.\n\nWhen we need to add a field in the future and are already spending the effort to bump the encoding version, we should definitely use add a bits used field.",
      "parentUuid": "245960bd_8ed1bc44",
